# Networking Concepts

SQL injection occurs at the application layer, but it still relies on the underlying network communication between the client and web server.

A simplified flow is:

```text
Browser
   |
   v
HTTP / HTTPS
   |
   v
Web Server
   |
   v
Web Application
   |
   v
SQL Query
   |
   v
Database
```

The user-controlled input travels within an HTTP request to the web application.

The application then interacts with the database.

The resulting database information, errors, or application behavior may affect the HTTP response returned to the client.

---

# HTTP and HTTPS

HTTP and HTTPS are application-layer protocols used for communication between web clients and web servers.

Common ports include:

```text
HTTP  → TCP Port 80
HTTPS → TCP Port 443
```

SQL injection targets how the web application handles input used within database queries.

HTTPS can protect network traffic while it is in transit, but encryption does not fix insecure SQL query construction inside the application.

